+# A02 frozen-input admission package
+
+This package requests distinct **import admission**, not A02 completion. No target
+repository has been assembled and no source has been imported. Final source is
+`nSealr/nsealr@f2ef70f522af4977e15f81554a8c6eadcdbe8097`, after S01 adoption and
+successful main CI `39152175828`. The coordinator holds product-source main fixed.
+The earlier provisional inventory and approved four-file `709f091` specification
+remain unchanged historical records.
+
+The exact selections and rights assessment are in
+[file-dispositions.json](admission-evidence/file-dispositions.json). Public source
+paths and selected CC0 private helper paths are explicit. Excluded private path
+names/bodies are absent; protected inventories and restored bundles preserve them.
+MIT notices remain for Bridge/Pi, CC0 notices for contracts and the 39 individually
+selected lab files. No competing nested notice or third-party copyright header
+was found in these new selections. Existing public nsealr ancestry retains its
+original vendor, official-vector and KiCad notices; its root MIT notice does not
+relicense those materials. The no-license private workspace/legacy hardware
+histories are recovery-only, with no selected import files.
+
+Private lab review found no production credentials in the selected helpers/tests.
+Example key/secret strings are intentional public test fixtures or rejection
+probes. Two helpers reference excluded private documents and therefore require
+the separately reviewed [privacy exception](privacy-addendum.md) before the first
+public import commit. Its public source records omit those document names. The
+original full patch stays protected. This author assessment still requires the
+whole-package independent rights/privacy review; a license marker or hash alone
+cannot establish permission or safe publication.
+
+This is the **initial selected-source admission map**, not a completed final
+transformation whitelist. A `retain` row requires unchanged source bytes in the
+initial import; it does not authorize an undeclared later edit. The accepted
+graph move also requires changes to live AGENTS/navigation/bootstrap paths and
+new current documents, host locks and artifact manifests. Each later addition,
+move or edit needs an explicit path, original hash where applicable, resulting
+hash and patch/declaration, with affected checks and review. Frozen historical
+evidence stays immutable. Final path correctness can only be demonstrated by
+the actual assembled candidate.
+
+The initial map explicitly retains the contract and Pi structure checkers required
+by existing tests/Makefiles. Their obsolete standalone-repository file lists will
+be adapted while preserving wrong-license, missing-directory and arbitrary
+checkout-name failures. The map also retires the card-only dev simulator and
+three card-only descriptors outside the smartcard vector directory. General
+policy-route mismatch checks remain and use retained routes.
+
+The original twenty integration obligations remain individually mapped in the
+approved brief: seventeen product obligations, one separately executed external
+hardware regression, and two explicit smartcard retirements. Four additional
+selected CC0 files retain the optional Chromium and serial smoke helpers and all
+thirteen existing mock safety tests. The actual installed-browser/attached-board
+smoke procedures remain unperformed and resource-gated. They do not become product
+build prerequisites or hardware support claims.
+
+## Before-state evidence and case obligations
+
+[Before-gate bindings](admission-evidence/before-gates.json) verify source pins,
+commands, log hashes and environments for all eight original software CI suites,
+plus the corrected uninterrupted twenty-step integration. Reuse is explicit:
+six unchanged suites retain the original S01 execution; core/lab and full
+integration use the fresh repaired S01 execution. All source pins except the
+documented core integration delta match the final tuple. Between tested core
+`7a32eed` and final `f2ef70f`, the only changes are restart documents/evidence and
+the separately accepted CAD tool addition. Rust, runtime controls, workflow and
+build commands are identical. The current complete graph validator and all
+eighteen controls were run directly on clean `f2ef70f`, with every bound file
+compared to Git before and after.
+
+The old/fresh local environment records match after replacing their declared
+runtime root; the actual Python and Node binaries match by SHA-256. All pinned
+versions, wheels, lockfiles and the original host boundary remain recorded.
+This is reused local before-state evidence, not a new cold installation or an
+OS-hermetic/hosted-CI guarantee. Earlier failures, including the original S01
+provenance bypass, remain immutable historical evidence; repaired final gates
+passed. No after-migration result is claimed from those logs.
+
+Actual framework collection at the exact existing S01 runtime yielded 716
+TypeScript, 92 contract-verifier, 150 Pi and 169 lab cases. Every tracked input,
+including four corrected lab overlay postimages, matched before and after
+collection. The Rust execution log supplies 263 distinct executed unit/vector/
+secret-boundary/doctest cases. Current unittest discovery adds the eighteen plan
+and eleven bootstrap cases. See the [case ledger](admission-evidence/case-dispositions.json)
+and [core Python collection](admission-evidence/core-python-cases.json).
+
+The ledger separates retained assertions, adapted active contracts, replacement
+artifact/retired-route negatives, external regression, smartcard retirement and
+the two retired private-prose assertions. The remaining twenty-five cases have [individual opaque dispositions](private-case-obligations.json): twenty-one preserve product/integration guardrails through mandatory replacements, and four obsolete private editorial/taxonomy assertions retire. Their exact IDs, paths and source hashes remain protected. Existing selected import/privacy controls support the public-to-test-only dependency boundary; they do not replace the missing production-source custody-claim, duplicate-validator ownership or stale CLI prose checks. Each replacement specifies both negative and positive controls, its owner/gate and actual after-import execution obligation. No private taxonomy or audit implementation is imported. The thirteen useful optional-helper cases are retained separately from this group.
+
+The complete after-migration acceptance remains mandatory:
+
+| Original boundary | Required target acceptance/disposition |
+| --- | --- |
+| Core `make ci` | Current graph/evidence validator and all controls at `plan/`; format, both clippy modes, core/default/std/doc/secret tests, simulator replay/category completeness, real RISC-V core build, dependency/license audit, coverage threshold and two-path reproducible builds. Split host/core workspaces and locks; do not weaken coverage or unify std accidentally. |
+| Companion `make ci` | Frozen pnpm install, build, complete retained Vitest cases, CLI/service/extension behavior, typecheck, consumer/examples/readme/API checks, API review, package registry, browser import/bundle, extension security, public imports, release plan/artifact safety, pack consumers and production dependency audit. Replace all-package publication assumptions with the single packed SDK; retain each useful check. |
+| Specs `make ci` | Independent Python verifier and retained negative cases, schema/vector/fixture inventory and provenance, wrong-license/missing-directory/renamed-root checks. No pre-test regeneration of expected values. |
+| Pi `make ci` | Pinned dependency install, all 150 unit cases with path adaptations, compile/dependency checks and independent event/signature/review/recovery oracles. Actual GPIO/camera/display procedures remain separate. |
+| Lab `make ci` and `make integration` | Full retained helper regressions and explicit replacements; one uninterrupted invocation of all seventeen product integration obligations. The original hardware audit/alignment regression runs separately against its exact external source. Retire only individually recorded card/private-editorial/taxonomy/prose cases; execute all replacement product guardrails. |
+| Hardware/website suites | Preserve their separate source owners, histories and before evidence. The external hardware regression still executes after migration; unchanged standalone website/CAD suites do not become product build prerequisites. |
+| Archived smartcard suite | Before evidence and public history preserved. No active card execution/import/public export/command; test explicit rejection of retired surfaces. |
+| New migration boundaries | Source equality and declared-delta checks, fixture/evidence tamper controls, two checkout locations, isolated packed SDK Node/browser/type consumers, no sibling hardware/SDK/private checkout, reproducible second assembly and candidate recovery. |
+
+Cases inside fixture loops are additionally bound by every source JSON blob in
+the file map. Only the card category and three card-only descriptors retire.
+Mixed feature matrix/route-refusal/schema members lose the card member explicitly;
+the general policy-route-mismatch fixture is adapted to a retained policy. All
+other expected cryptographic/protocol values remain independent. T01 may later
+introduce the separately reviewed capability/profile contract; this migration
+does not create an additional normative profile owner.
+
+## Evidence, recovery and source admission
+
+[Closed evidence](admission-evidence/closed-evidence.json) covers all 1,511 artifact
+references and 1,508 unique files from seven integrated tasks. All current hashes,
+manifest bindings and historical relative links resolve at the frozen source.
+The future `plan/evidence-index.json` is derived navigation/equivalence only.
+Frozen artifact bytes/paths stay unchanged. Editable current P01 contracts receive
+separate source-equivalence records and one current normative path each. No old
+graph placeholder, second state ledger or rewritten review hash is permitted.
+
+All twelve source bundles were actually verified and restored in protected
+storage; every captured ref object and selected tree matched, and all twelve
+`git fsck --full --strict` commands passed. The workspace receipt-only move to
+`5127d94` was preserved by an additional restore, without changing its historical
+selected pin or publishing its paths/history. Recovery logs/ref inventories and
+objects remain private. Public summaries report hashes and counts only.
+The subsequently prepared hardware verifier branch was also captured/restored
+in a separate protected refresh; it does not change selected hardware main or
+claim adoption. These records bind the refs observed at each capture, not an
+assertion that unrelated development refs never advance.
+
+Those all-ref bundles are backups, not public target intake. Actual assembly must
+initialize an empty target and fetch only exact public core `f2ef70f` ancestry
+without local hardlinks/alternates or implicit tags. Never plain-clone the shared
+canonical object store into the target. Check reachable commits and all target
+objects against public core ancestry plus explicit new source/transform commits;
+selected CC0 file blobs are allowed, private source commit histories are not.
+Add a synthetic unselected-private-branch/object negative to the implemented
+assembly path. Keep the protected full backups intact.
+
+All nine observed public mains equal the chosen exact pins; reviewed evidence
+tags match remote objects and are not product release tags. The new negative
+control rejects an advanced main even when the selected commit remains its
+ancestor. Repeat exact current-ref and source correspondence checks immediately
+before and after eventual import. Any new main/source input, including S03,
+requires reconciliation; never replay an older wholesale tree over new modules.
+
+The current workflow's `actions/checkout@v5`, `actions/setup-python@v6` and
+`ubuntu-latest` are mutable external inputs. When implementing the consolidated
+workflow, resolve any chosen action pins from exact official upstream source
+with version comments and run affected CI. Evaluate `push.branches: [main]`,
+`pull_request` and manual dispatch to avoid duplicate branch/PR checks while
+preserving required verify/application jobs and actual main post-merge CI.
+
+The only next authorization gate is distinct review of this exact completed
+admission package plus the coordinator's record. After that, actual import,
+transformation, complete target execution, recovery/reproduction and distinct
+final review still have to occur. No physical resource or release acceptance is
+closed by this preparation package.
